   "claims": [
    "For example, if your last cycle started on November 16th, and it typically lasts for 29 days, you can expect the next period to begin on December 15th.",
    "For a five-day-long period, you can expect the bleeding to stop on December 19th.",
    "Pre period, also known as premenstrual syndrome (PMS), is a syndrome that up to 90% of women will experience in their reproductive lives.",
    "Take your average cycle duration, subtract 14 days from this value, and add the remaining number of days to the date your last period began.",
    "Periods may last anywhere between 3 and 8 days, but they usually last for 5 days.",
    "Girls generally get their first period around the age of 10-12, although it can happen as early as 8.",
    "The chances of getting pregnant during your period are increased if your menstrual cycle is less than 28 days, as your ovulation day is closer to your period.",
    "The amount of blood lost during a period will vary from woman to woman, but, on average, a woman will lose about 6-8 teaspoons (30-40 ml) of blood per period.",
    "A loss of 80 ml or more, having a period longer than seven days, or both, is considered heavy."
   ],
