   "claims": [
    "See a forecast of your upcoming periods with a 12-month period calendar based on your cycle history.",
    "We provide a calendar feature that shows a preview of your expected period dates 3 months at a time, ahead or in the past.",
    "You can also print a list or calendar view of your expected period dates for the next 12 months.",
    "Count from day 1 of one period up until day 1 of the next.",
    "Example period date calculation: If your last period started on January 1 and your cycle is 29 days long, your next period should start around January 30.",
    "Add your cycle length to the first day of your last period January 1 + 29 Days = January 30 Why Use a Period Calculator Knowing when to expect your period can help you plan for upcoming events or travel.",
    "Typically ovulation occurs around 14 days before the start of your next period.",
    "Just subtract 14 days from your expected period date."
   ],
